<title>MEXICO: Vitro sells raw materials arm for $131 mln.</title>
<headline>Vitro sells raw materials arm for $131 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican glassmaker Vitro, S.A., said on Thursday it had reached a preliminary deal whereby U.S. industrial minerals company Unimin Corp. would acquire 100 percent of Vitro's raw materials division for approximately $131 million in cash.</p>
<p>Vitro also signed a 10-year agreement for Unimin to supply &quot;practically all&quot; of its silica sand and feldspar requirements, a company statement said.</p>
